<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Takua Pa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Takua Pa is a town and district in Phang Nga Province on the Andaman Sea coast of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>. In the first millennium CE the area, especially the island of Ko Kho Khao, was a port on the route across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>. A ninth-century Tamil inscription found there names a merchant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guild</a> and a tank named after a title of the Pallava king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nandivarman-iii">Nandivarman III</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/takua-pa.jpg" alt="Takua Pa" width="320" height="458" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hdamm based on Amphoe Phang Nga.svg · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amphoe_8205.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
